      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.1 Constitutional and Legal Status"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 371(H) lays down important constitutional provisions specific to state administration.",
        "The Inner Line Permit (ILP) serves as a critical regulatory mechanism for legal status and entry regulation.",
        "Local self-government encompasses both statutory Panchayati Raj Institutions and traditional governance bodies like the Kebang.",
        "The Arunachal Pradesh Public Service Commission (APPSC) manages civil service recruitment and public administration affairs."
      ],
      "id": "sav2wr5"
    },
